    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI released **version 2 of the owner identity**, satisfying every part of the spec:\n\n**Version\u20112 identifier derivation** \u2014 a fixed `\"V2\"` tag is now mixed into the hash input of each identifier, so all three change and no version\u20111 value is reproduced:\n- `MemberId` (`util/MemberId.java`): `HASH8 = sha256(\"V2\" + region + telephone + lastName)[:8]`. The **plain region still leads the id** (`NSW\u2026`), so it remains extractable.\n- `HouseholdNormalizer.toHouseholdId`: `sha256(\"V2\" + comparisonKey)[:12]` \u2014 matching semantics unchanged.\n- `OwnerIdentity.identityKey`: prepends `\"V2|\"` to the hashed input \u2014 duplicate\u2011detection semantics unchanged (both sides V2).\n\n**Locality stays plain** \u2014 `locality`, `timezone`, and the owner segment's region still read the plain region prefix off the member id, so they report `NSW` (never a `V2` tag). The `V2` tag lives only inside the identifiers.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` \u2192 regenerated DTOs, `OwnerMapper`):\n- New nested `identity` object groups `memberId`, `identityKey`, `householdId`; those three are removed from the top level.\n- New top\u2011level integer `apiVersion` = `2`.\n\n**Audit event** (`OwnerCreatedEvent`, controller builder): moved to schema version 2 \u2014 added `schemaVersion: 2` and the owner segment recomputed from the version\u20112 identity: `{seq, ownerId, memberId, membershipLevel, ownerSegment, schemaVersion, event}`.\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) are untouched. The runtime audit line confirms the shape: `{\"seq\":1,...,\"memberId\":\"NSW27DD5C34098\",\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\",\"schemaVersion\":2,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` \u2014 plain `NSW` prefix retained, V2 hash applied.",
