    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, in-order sequence for `POST /api/owners` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, lines 185\u2013230), with the security check that precedes it.\n\n## Pre-flight\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`: caller must hold the owner-admin role (line 183).\n- **Bean Validation** on the request body (`OwnerFieldsDto`) runs before the method body \u2014 rejects null/empty required fields and any field-level patterns declared in the DTO. The method's own guards exist to close gaps this leaves (e.g. whitespace-only values).\n\n## In `addOwner`, in execution order\n\n**1. Idempotency replay (short-circuit side-effect)** \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header (line 186). If that key was already recorded and its owner still exists, it returns that original owner with `200 OK` and does nothing else (lines 187\u2013195).\n\n**2. `normalizeAddress` (side-effect)** \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and the flat `address` in place on the DTO; the composed value becomes the canonical address all later steps judge (line 196).\n\n**3. `rejectBlankOwnerFields` (validation \u2192 400)** \u2014 requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, an address (`addressLine1` or flat `address`), `city`, and `telephone` (line 197).\n\n**4. `rejectInvalidPostcode` (validation \u2192 400)** \u2014 postcode is optional; if present it must be 4 digits and within the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) (line 198).\n\n**5. `normalizeTelephone` (validation + side-effect)** \u2014 normalizes telephone to canonical form, writing it back; rejects with 400 if it can't be normalized (line 199).\n\n**6. `normalizeEmail` (validation + side-effect)** \u2014 if email present, normalizes and writes it back; rejects 400 on invalid syntax or a disposable-domain blocklist hit; absent/blank is left untouched (line 200).\n\n**7. `householdIdFor` (compute)** \u2014 derives household id from `lastName` + `postcode` (line 201).\n\n**8. Read `sharesHousehold` flag** (line 202).\n\n**9. `rejectDuplicateIdentity` (validation \u2192 409)** \u2014 computes the derived identity key `sha256(normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))` and rejects if any active (non-deleted) owner already carries it (line 203).\n\n**10. `countOwnersInCity` (compute)** \u2014 case-insensitive count of existing owners in the city (line 204).\n\n**11. `rejectCityAtCapacity` (validation \u2192 409)** \u2014 rejects if the city already holds \u2265 50 owners (line 205).\n\n**12. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` (validation \u2192 400)** \u2014 rejects if the supplied registration date is after today (line 206).\n\n**13. `effectiveRegistrationDate` (compute)** \u2014 defaults to today if omitted, then rolls a weekend date forward to Monday (line 207).\n\n**14. `countRegisteredOn` (compute)** \u2014 counts owners already registered on that effective date (line 208).\n\n**15. `rejectDailyRegistrationLimitReached` (validation \u2192 429)** \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners already carry that day's registration date (line 209).\n\n## Building and stamping the owner (side-effects on the new entity)\n\n**16. `ownerMapper.toOwner`** maps the DTO to an `Owner` (line 211), then the controller stamps:\n- `registrationDate` = effective date (line 212)\n- `householdId` (line 213)\n- `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with same first+last name, case-insensitive (line 214)\n- `bulkSignupWarning` = `registeredThatDay > 80` (line 215)\n- `capacityWarning` = `ownersInCity >= 40` (line 216)\n- `householdSize` = existing household members + 1 (line 217)\n- `membershipLevel` = the mapper's level, **capped** at `max(household members' level) + 1` (line 218)\n- `markPossibleDuplicate` (line 219) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, finds the oldest active owner sharing postcode + Soundex(lastName) but a different identity key, and sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\n## Persistence and post-create side-effects\n\n**17. `clinicService.saveOwner` (persist + side-effect)** \u2014 on a new owner with no member id, **generates the member id** `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (Luhn check digit), deduplicating with a `-<n>` suffix on collision, then saves (lines 220; service 239\u2013262).\n\n**18. Record idempotency key** \u2014 maps the header key to the new owner's id for future replay (lines 221\u2013223).\n\n**19. `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`** \u2014 maps to the response DTO (line 224), deriving `membershipLevel` and `ownerSegment`.\n\n**20. `emitOwnerCreatedAudit` (side-effect)** \u2014 writes a human-readable `AUDIT` log line, then a structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON line; bumps the global `EVENT_SEQ` counter exactly once (line 225).\n\n**21. `enqueueWelcomeNotification` (side-effect)** \u2014 writes a `NOTIFY` log line carrying owner id + member id (line 226).\n\n**22. Set `Location` header** to `/api/owners/{id}` and return `201 Created` with the DTO (lines 227\u2013229).\n\nNote the two identity/duplicate checks in step 9 and the possible-duplicate mark in step 16, plus the city (11) and daily (15) limits, are all evaluated against `clinicService.findAllOwners()` read live at each step \u2014 there is no single transactional snapshot across them, and `addOwner` itself is not `@Transactional`."
